! Athenaion ~ Hard External Research Reference

The Operator designated `Leonxlnx/athenaion` a ''hard source reference'' for
Projection Loom's intent-generalized, seed-independent architectural growth.
Consult and compare its pinned source in future planning and implementation.
This hard reference does NOT grant authority to Athenaion's geometry, aesthetic
choices, camera calibration, execution model, or Elyncia canon.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/provenance>>

!! Pin, License and Witness Scope

* ''Repository:'' https://github.com/Leonxlnx/athenaion
* ''Pinned commit:'' `9b8bd23b39c458a50fb1201037360047781c45b5`, inspected 2026-10-27 from public GitHub.
* ''License:'' MIT, copyright (c) 2026 Leon Lin. Retain the source notice
  when reusing substantial software; no copied code enters this meme.
* ''Inspected works:'' README, `docs/ART_BIBLE.md`, `docs/COMPOSITION.md`,
  `docs/CONTRACT.md`, `src/world/layout.js`, `src/world/index.js`,
  `src/core/engine.js`, `src/core/rng.js`, `src/core/footprints.js`,
  `src/arch/build.js`, `src/modules/acropolis.js`,
  `src/terrain/erosion.js`, and `tools/render.mjs`.
* ''Read as:'' a procedural Three.js world with nine AI-generated visual
  references and an author-reported multi-agent composition/render process;
  no independent verification of its 4K/agent-hour/quality claims here.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/transfer>>

!! Concrete Architecture Rhymes

* ''Shared layout, moving dependents.'' One scene-owned spatial plan drives
  terrain, architecture, stairs, terraces, city and cameras. Loom SHOULD
  compose subject-neutral location/frame relationships, not hard-code a
  Necrospire or Athenaion coordinate master.
* ''Sites publish opportunities.'' Athenaion's building/engine slots and
  footprints let later modules place statues, ivy, trees and props around
  already built sites. Loom SHOULD generate typed structural bearing sockets,
  decorative slots and occupancy/route zones independently; a footprint check
  MUST NOT impersonate a native BRep contact or traversability certificate.
* ''Modules submit to two tests.'' Independent `build(engine)` and
  `test(engine)` run beside whole-world render comparisons. Loom SHOULD
  audition each capability alone and then in composed native location space.
* ''Image groups constrain one world.'' Nine source references invite camera
  and landmark fits, view-by-view diagnostics and an art bible. Every source
  keeps its own camera/registration evidence; RGB and alpha of one image
  remain one entity. Synthetic views inspect, never become new source images.
* ''Deterministic local variation.'' Named RNG and resource-tiered rendering
  suggest keyed random substreams and bounded coarse-to-fine rendering for
  independently reproducible epochs.
* ''No shot-specific hidden construction.'' Athenaion's `onShot` hooks allow
  presentation changes. Loom MUST preserve identical construction/void/genome
  truth across camera views; any shot-varying structural geometry requires a
  new explicit candidate and independent audits.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/limits>>

Athenaion does not demonstrate native BRep validation, autonomous genetic
lineage selection, certified multi-view photogrammetry, a generic intent
contract or idempotent OODA-HA replay. Its no-external-assets constraint
belongs to that project, not to a general-purpose Projection Loom.

All 20 planned generalization items and the image-group / brutalist grammar /
ziggurat-proxy seven-combination Experiment Zero matrix live in
the current `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/projection-loom-handoff`; the retired comparison and roadmap remain recoverable from `archive/pr84-markdown-pre-otakiage-20261031`.
Neither document claims the new functionality already executed.

<<~/ahu>>

